== Advanced Survival

=== Traversal Efficiency

- [*Fast travel network:*] In Wave 1 you should unlock all stagecoach
  stations and train routes early. Combine with camp fast travel for
  near-instant movement across the map
- [*Horse rotation:*] Keep 2-3 horses at camp. Use a war horse (Turkoman,
  Ardennes) for combat zones and a race horse (Arabian, Missouri Fox
  Trotter) for traversing long distances. Switch at camp or stables
- [*Waypoint chaining:*] Set a waypoint to the farthest destination, then
  set intermediate waypoints at stables and fence locations along the
  route — never backtrack

=== Weather and Environment

- [*Cold weather:*] New Hanover and Ambarino drain your health core if
  Arthur isn't wearing cold-weather gear. Keep a warm outfit (sheepskin
  jacket, gloves, hat) on your horse
- [*Bayou:*] Saint Denis and Lagras have high disease risk. Eat cooked
  food (not raw) and sleep in hotels to reset
- [*Night:*] Enemies have lower vision at night. Use the cover of darkness
  for stealth approaches and train robberies

== Playstyle Suggestions

=== The Highwayman

Focus on stagecoach and train robberies. Hit the Cornwall Kerosene &
Tar coach outside Valentine for early capital. Graduate to the train
tunnel near Riggs Station for an ambush that lawmen can't easily reach.
Spend profits on the best horses and weapons — reinvest in crime.

=== The Land Baron

Live off the land. Hunt legendary animals, craft everything at the Trapper,
sell surplus meat and pelts. Invest the proceeds in the camp and stable
upgrades. Only engage in story missions when you need a change of pace.
_Suggested challenge:_ Go 10 in-game days without entering a town.

=== The Bounty Killer

Target only bounty missions and legendary bounties. Bring every target in
alive for double payout + honor gain. Use the reinforced lasso and bounty
wagon to transport multiple targets. Build reputation as the most feared
bounty hunter in the West — then betray the law when Wave 1's outlaw mods
make crime more profitable.

=== The Collector

100% completion run. Hunt every cigarette card, dinosaur bone, dreamcatcher,
rock carving, and grave. Use the compendium to track progress. This
playstyle rewards patience and thorough exploration — the game hides its
best secrets in the farthest corners of the map.

=== The Menace

Maximum chaos. Low honor from Chapter 2. Rob every store, hold up every
stagecoach, kill witnesses before they report you. Never pay off a bounty
— let the bounty hunters come. Fight them for the XP and loot. _Suggested
challenge:_ Survive a 5-star wanted level in Saint Denis for 5 minutes.

=== Roleplaying Prompts

- Play through the game without using the mini-map — navigate by road
  signs, landmarks, and the sun
- Change Arthur's outfit to match the region you're in (cold gear in
  Ambarino, light clothes in Lemoyne)
- Stay in hotels instead of sleeping at camp when you're "on a job"
- Only save the game at campsites or hotels — no quick-save
- If Arthur dies, drop \$100 from your cash (a "hospital bill")

== Save Management

Wave 1 mods change game mechanics. Keep backups:

```default
Documents/Rockstar Games/RDR2/Profiles/
├── wave0_backup/       <- before Wave 1 install
├── wave1_ch2.sav       <- Chapter 2 checkpoint
├── wave1_ch4.sav       <- Chapter 4 checkpoint
└── wave1_ch6.sav       <- Endgame checkpoint
```

== Performance Tuning

Heavy mod loads impact performance. Recommended settings:

- [*Resolution:*] 1920x1080 or 2560x1440 (not 4K with heavy graphics mods)
- [*Texture Quality:*] Ultra
- [*Reflection Quality:*] Medium
- [*Water Quality:*] Medium
- [*Volumetrics:*] Low
- [*Tree Tessellation:*] Off
